     "Buddha",
     "Mahavira",
     "ahimsa"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Buddhism began with Gautama Buddha, who taught the middle path, the four noble truths and compassion. Jainism, with teachers like Mahavira, teaches ahimsa, truth and non-possession.\nBoth arose in India about 2,500 years ago and spread widely. Folk and tribal traditions honour nature, trees and local gods through songs, dances and festivals.\nThese belief systems influenced one another and enriched Indian culture."
    }
